%description:

Tcp.increasedIWEnabled:conflict -- with initialWindow "rfc6928", the deprecated parameter stops the run with an error.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "an error with initialWindow = "rfc6928"".

The classes: off (false, the default), on (true: initialWindow "rfc3390") and conflict (true
with initialWindow "rfc6928": an error). The code: TcpConnection::configureStateVariables().

Host under test: host1, with initialWindow "rfc6928". Observation: the error, and the exit code
of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.increasedIWEnabled
%# class: conflict
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.increasedIWEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpIncreasedIWEnabledConflict compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.increasedIWEnabled = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.initialWindow = "rfc6928"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
set either the deprecated increasedIWEnabled or initialWindow
